{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.c1_undetermined_at_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.c1_undetermined_at_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.lean#L165-L173","doc":"The two halves joined: at the fibre-monodromy value `q = -1`, C1's leading\ncoefficient vanishes for every **even** index, so on that whole subsequence the carrier\ndetermines nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.c1_undetermined_of_qint_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.c1_undetermined_of_qint_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.lean#L154-L163","doc":"**A vanishing leading coefficient makes C1 a constraint, not a recurrence.**\n\nIf `[n+2]_q = 0` then the C1 equation holds for one candidate value of `b_{n+2}` iff it\nholds for every candidate value — so it carries no information about `b_{n+2}`. This is\nindependent of the carrier theorem's hypothesis; it is what that hypothesis exists to\nprevent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.c1_hypothesis_fails_at_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.c1_hypothesis_fails_at_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.lean#L143-L152","doc":"**The C1 carrier's standing hypothesis is FALSE at `q = -1`.**\n\n`QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.qlift_normalized_kernel_exists` — the proved binding\nq-difference carrier `[n+2]_q·b_{n+2} = b_{n+1} + b_n` — assumes\n`∀ k, 1 ≤ k → qint q k ≠ 0`. At the value route 2's fibre monodromy supplies, that\nassumption does not hold, so the carrier theorem does not apply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.qint_neg_one_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.qint_neg_one_two","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.lean#L138-L141","doc":"The instance that matters: `[2]_{-1} = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.qint_neg_one_two_mul_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.qint_neg_one_two_mul_succ","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.lean#L129-L136","doc":"At `q = -1` the **odd** quantum integers are `1`: `[2k+1]_{-1} = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.qint_neg_one_two_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.qint_neg_one_two_mul","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.lean#L113-L127","doc":"At `q = -1` the **even** quantum integers vanish: `[2k]_{-1} = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.colorCubic_no_triple_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.colorCubic_no_triple_root","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FibreMonodromyOrderTwo.lean#L81-L107","doc":"**No total branch point.** If the colour cubic `X³ + (z+1)X² + (z²+z+1)X +\n(z³+z²+z+1)` equalled `(X − r)³` — i.e. if all three sheets collided over `z` — its\ncoefficients would satisfy the three hypotheses below. They are inconsistent, for every\n`z` and every `r`.\n\nConsequently every branch point of the 3-sheeted cover is **simple**: exactly two\nsheets meet, so the local monodromy is a transposition of order `2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}